{
    "_comment": [
        "Multi-Host VCS Topology (CXL r3.2 Section 7.6.6 compliant)",
        "",
        "Demonstrates Virtual CXL Switch (VCS) partitioning for multi-host access.",
        "Per CXL spec, Multiple VCS requires multiple Upstream Ports (USPs).",
        "Each VCS has its own USP connecting to a different host.",
        "",
        "Physical Layout:",
        "  Switch (cxl_switch_0)",
        "    USP0 (port 0) - upstream to Host A / Root Port 0",
        "    USP1 (port 1) - upstream to Host B / Root Port 1",
        "    DSP0 (port 2) - SLD dev0 (32GB)  -> VCS0",
        "    DSP1 (port 3) - SLD dev1 (32GB)  -> VCS0",
        "    DSP2 (port 4) - SLD dev2 (64GB)  -> VCS1",
        "    DSP3 (port 5) - MLD (4 LDs x 32GB = 128GB)",
        "                      LD0 -> VCS0/Host A",
        "                      LD1 -> VCS0/Host A",
        "                      LD2 -> VCS1/Host B",
        "                      LD3 -> VCS1/Host B",
        "",
        "VCS Configuration (per CXL vPPB Ordering: USP vPPB first, then DSP vPPBs):",
        "  VCS0 (Host A): 64GB SLD (dev0+dev1) + 64GB MLD (LD0+LD1) = 128GB",
        "    vPPB0 -> USP (bound to Port 0, implicit)",
        "    vPPB1 -> BoundPhysicalPort: DSP0/Port 2 (dev0)",
        "    vPPB2 -> BoundPhysicalPort: DSP1/Port 3 (dev1)",
        "    vPPB3 -> BoundLD: DSP3/Port 5/LD0",
        "    vPPB4 -> BoundLD: DSP3/Port 5/LD1",
        "",
        "  VCS1 (Host B): 64GB SLD (dev2) + 64GB MLD (LD2+LD3) = 128GB",
        "    vPPB0 -> USP (bound to Port 1, implicit)",
        "    vPPB1 -> BoundPhysicalPort: DSP2/Port 4 (dev2)",
        "    vPPB2 -> BoundLD: DSP3/Port 5/LD2",
        "    vPPB3 -> BoundLD: DSP3/Port 5/LD3",
        "    vPPB4 -> Unbound (available for future binding)",
        "",
        "Key Concepts Demonstrated:",
        "  - Multiple USPs: Each VCS has its own upstream port to its host",
        "  - vPPB #0 is always the USP vPPB (per CXL vPPB Ordering)",
        "  - BoundPhysicalPort: vPPB bound to entire device (SLD or PCIe)",
        "  - BoundLD: vPPB bound to specific LD within MLD (memory partitioning)",
        "  - Unbound: vPPB available for dynamic binding via FM-API",
        "  - Each VCS appears as independent switch to its host"
    ],
